{#
  Single source of truth for closest-city weather data.

  Consumers: closest_city_sensor (configuration.yaml) and automations.
  Usage in any template:
      {% from 'cities.jinja' import closest_cities %}
      {% set cities = closest_cities() | from_json %}

  After editing this file, reload without restarting Home Assistant:
      Developer Tools > Actions > homeassistant.reload_custom_templates

  The macro body must stay a single valid JSON object (it is piped
  through | tojson and consumed with from_json). No comments inside it.

  ============================================================
  HOW TO ADD A CITY
  ============================================================

  CASE A - city already listed below with lat/lon only
  (~37 of the entries: detection works, weather shows 'unknown'):

    1. UI: Settings > Devices & Services > Add Integration
       - Canada: "Environment Canada" -> creates weather.<city>_forecast
         AND all sensor.<city>_* entities automatically.
       - Elsewhere: "Met.no" -> creates ONLY weather.forecast_<city>.
    2. Here: add the entity keys to that city's entry (see field list).
    3. CASE CANADA ONLY - you are done.
       CASE MET.NO ONLY: also clone the Boston block of derived sensors
       in configuration.yaml (sensor.boston_current_condition etc.) and
       adjust names to the new city.
    4. Reload Custom Templates (+ Template Entities if you added
       derived sensors). Weather fields light up automatically;
       sensor.closest_city needs no other change.

  CASE B - brand-new city (not in the list at all):

    1. Add the weather integration as above.
    2. (Met.no: derived sensors as above.)
    3. Add a full entry below with curated coordinates.
       Curated coords are deliberate: coordinates stored by some
       integrations are wrong/unreliable.

  ============================================================
  FIELDS PER CITY
  ============================================================
    lat/lon     coordinates used for nearest-city detection
    weather     weather.* entity id
    condition / temperature / high / low / summary
                present once a weather source exists
    humidex / uv_index / wind_chill / warnings
                Environment Canada cities only

    Omit any key that does not exist yet - every consumer falls
    back to 'unknown', and weather automations skip 'unknown'
    cities silently.
#}
{% macro closest_cities() -%}
